      "writtenOn": "2023-10-23T20:13:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like the Pipeline isn\u0027t a great place to be storing this cache and this would make more sense to be on the DawnResourceProvider. In those model we end up with a different cache on every pipeline. I would assume we\u0027d want to use bind group objects across different pipelines? But maybe the need to pass in the uniform buffer size makes that difficult to do?\n\nLooks like the only thing we need from the Pipeline here are the two UniformTotalBytes. Could we just query those off of the pipeline and pass those into a call on the ResourceCache?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 681,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 681,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b77a5b02_bbe94e19",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 681,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-23T20:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The bind groups can be used across different pipelines. However it will need to be compatible with the pipeline\u0027s bind group layout. The layout is one parameter used to create the bind group. Currently we create a separate bind group layout for each pipeline. So storing the cached bind group per pipeline helps avoid using the bind group layout as a cache key\u0027s component helping reducing the key\u0027s size.\n\nDawn actually caches the bind group layouts internally, so creating group layouts with same descriptor twice might return the same object. However Dawn doesn\u0027t provide API to know that it is cached. We will need an additional hash table in order to know that. So if we want to store the cache inside DawnResourceProvider, we will need to include the bind group layout as part of the key.\n\nOne thing about caching bind groups at high level layer is that we will also need high level abstraction of the bind group layouts.",
      "parentUuid": "1fe5878f_94ed3d19",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 681,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 681,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ecb6cf73_aefdc9e6",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 681,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T13:47:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Dawn does a pipeline just have a single bind group layout that has all the bind group entries for the whole pipeline? Like in Ganesh Vulkan we do cache DescriptorSets but don\u0027t need to worry about the full PipelineLayout. The reason is we decided that in all PipelineLayouts DescriptorSet 0 will contain the uniform buffers, and every pipeline uses the same number of uniform buffers (or at least has bindings for them even if unused). In that world it doesn\u0027t matter what the reset of the descriptor layout for a pipline is (e.g. number of samplers). So the reuse of these descriptors can be much broader across pipelines.\n\nMy quick scanning of the code does make me think that Dawn is setup similar. So to use the same model do we just need to make sure all pipelines use a similar uniform layout even with unused bindings?",
      "parentUuid": "b77a5b02_bbe94e19",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 681,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 681,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8573dfe_cb594fec",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 681,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T14:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Greg\u0027s initial thought that we should keep caching in the ResourceCache/ResourceProvider to be consistent with where everything else is accumulated.\n\nI feel less strongly about trying to reuse a BindGroup across pipelines, so we could keep the key small by using the resource unique ID of the GraphicsPipeline. Since the BindGroupLayout has concatenated the paint and the render step uniforms together, it\u0027s unlikely we\u0027d see reuse of BindGroups between different drawcalls that used the same SkPaint.\n\nHowever, where we could see reuse in BindGroups and layouts is when we make new pipelines because the RenderPassDesc changed but the paint and the renderstep are unchanged. In this case, if we have the `GraphicsPipelineDesc` available, it should be much closer to 1-to-1 with the bind group layout and is only 64-bits.",
      "parentUuid": "ecb6cf73_aefdc9e6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 681,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 681,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6691456_37afd073",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnGraphicsPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 681,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T19:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think Dawn also supports creating layout that is compatible with different pipelines even if the layout has more entries than what the pipeline needs. So creating a single layout for multiple pipelines sounds good to me.",
      "parentUuid": "f8573dfe_cb594fec",
      "range": {
