      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T14:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are `wgpu::BindGroup` objects ref-counted light weight objects? Or should we be returning a reference to the group that was stored in the cache?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 724,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 724,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e3b0e2a_2be20ff0",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnGraphicsPipeline.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T14:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could be simplified to be specific to the binding structure the base `GraphicsPipeline` expects and just stores 3 pointers to DawnBuffers for the intrinsic, renderstep, and paint uniforms.\n\nThis also means that the bind group key can be reduced to 3 unique IDs, since their order (assuming nulls are filled in with 0) encodes the bind index.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5dc6b5dd_0352fae8",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnGraphicsPipeline.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T14:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t need to be a unique pointer if we are always going to have a cache, then we save on indirection.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "928ca24c_228bc218",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnResourceWithSerial.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T14:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m was a little surprised that the base Graphite class doesn\u0027t have a unique ID on it. While they have a GrResourceKey on them, I don\u0027t think that is the right place to track uniqueness since we want different Resources with the same key to be equivalent from a ResourceProvider POV.\n\nBut a unique ID seems generally useful IMO; right now we just do pointer comparisons for bindings in DrawPass because we know everything is kept alive throughout and don\u0027t have to worry about a new resource being allocated in the same memory location. Even so, an id lets us have a safer comparison here, and may be useful in the future.\n\n@Greg WDYT about just moving this to the base Resource?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3da4c3367105a0860df18212104628a177329e94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
